a('No year was excluded as obsolete. This is a six-year, one-annual-series-per-year corpus, not a multi-variant sample. The 2022/2023 question filenames say First Proof; final-print equivalence is unconfirmed. Full local paths, hashes and report ranges are in `curriculum/source-inventory.json`; extraction page boundaries and hashes are in `assessment-evidence/extraction-manifest.json`.\n')
a(f"All 240 MC items and 382 marked structured/practical segments were read and mapped by meaning: **622 demands and 960 printed marks**. Twelve P2/P3 totals reconcile individually to 80/40. A segment is a terminal printed tariff: it may group several blanks or embedded subparts, and is not necessarily one rubric point. All mappings are lead-agent judgements against 335 syllabus source bullets plus one explicitly bounded Annex D diode-symbol anchor; they are not an independent review or a final decomposed target registry. There was no token-matched first pass.\n")
a('The 2024 MC question 9 has no correct option; the examiner compensated everyone (report PDF p.654). It stays in the census but is excluded from usable exposure: **621 demands, 959 marks**. Key/commentary/inference labels remain separate. The 2021–2025 reports supply 200 key-table entries: 199 usable answers and one compensation marker. **2020 Paper 1 contributes demands only, with no difficulty or answer evidence.** No 2020 MC key is held.\n')
a(f"Reports yield {s['commentary_blocks']} preserved native-text commentary blocks, {s['linked_blocks']} linked by exact, parent or whole-question references to demands; the remaining {s['commentary_blocks']-s['linked_blocks']} are general observations. {s['records_with_findings']} demand records have findings, {s['records_with_error_triage']} carry error-triage flags. These are blocks and potentially overlapping flags, not a sentence census, frequency of wrong beliefs, or a fully manually adjudicated classification of every clause. {len(mis)} genuine conceptual distinctions have been manually curated separately.\n")
a('Image-based marking tables were recovered with OCR on 55 report pages. OCR remains a draft extraction; the specifically read marking rows are now labelled `manually_checked_OCR_table` or `native_table_text`. All 137 primary calculate/define/explain demands are covered, including every one of the 25 three-mark calculations. The answer-shape register contains '+str(len(sh))+' distinct demand-level marking entries. Unrepresented task families remain a stated coverage gap.\n')
a('## 2. What each paper looks like')
a('\n| Paper | Corpus structure | Marks and principal demands |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 40 four-option MC items per year | 40 marks; concepts, quantitative reasoning and diagram/data reading. The option choice does not establish a written-answer marking architecture. |\n| 2 | 8–12 numbered structured questions, 37–47 marked segments per year | 80 marks; calculations, precise statements/definitions, explanations, diagrams and data interpretation. |\n| 3 | Five numbered questions in 2020; four in each later year; 17–25 marked segments | 40 marks; written practical skills using apparatus drawings, readings, tables, graphs, conclusions, errors and an eight-mark investigation plan. |\n')
a('P2 tariffs across 261 segments: '+', '.join(f'{k} mark(s): {v}' for k,v in sorted(collections.Counter(r['mark_tariff'] for r in rs if r['paper_id']=='2').items()))+'. Thus 253/261 (96.9%) carry 1–3 marks; the maximum is six. P3 has 121 segments, mostly one or two marks, five graph-sized five-mark tasks and six eight-mark plans. Those plans alone account for 48/240 practical marks, **20%**.\n')
a('On P2, **calculate is the largest single family**, carrying 173/480 marks (36.0%), **state** 67 (14.0%), **draw** 39 (8.1%), **explain** 35 (7.3%) and **describe** 33 (6.9%). Calculate plus determine carry 189/480 (39.4%). These counts allocate a grouped segment to its primary verb; they do not isolate every secondary instruction. Paper 3 is a written practical assessment, so cards and worked examples can prepare its interpretation and planning demands, but the examiner repeatedly calls for real practical experience too.\n')
a('The working syllabus gives Paper 2 as 1 h 30 min and Paper 3 as 1 h 15 min. Paper 1 remains recorded as 45 minutes in the syllabus and the 2020/2022–2024 covers, versus one hour on the 2021/2025 covers. This is the operator-waived non-major discrepancy; no 2026 examination duration is inferred.\n')
a('## 3. Command words actually used')
a('\nOne primary imperative per marked P2/P3 segment, including inherited parent instructions. Three interrogative segments have no imperative; MC questions remain null rather than being assigned “what” or “which”. Secondary verbs are not separately counted. A source typo in calculate is normalised with its source spelling retained in the demand review.\n')
