a('\nThe small primary share for Scientific processes does not mean those skills are unimportant: units, handling data and practical reasoning are embedded across topics, and practical marks are deliberately not included in that denominator. These primary-topic shares are not a per-mark AO decomposition.\n')
a('Outcomes linked in **all six years** include scalar/vector distinctions, motion-graph interpretation and area, specific-heat calculations, wave speed/period, refractive index, series/parallel resistance, decay-equation notation and half-life calculations. Graph axes/scales, best-fit lines, gradients, practical conclusions, controls and improvements recur across the practical corpus. See the generated exposure register for each source bullet, exact demand IDs, series, tariffs and command mix.\n')
a('Across 335 source bullets plus the Annex D anchor: '+', '.join(f'{v} {k}' for k,v in sorted(s['exposure_classes'].items()))+'. Here frequent means three or more usable years, occasional two, rare one and unseen zero; these thresholds are our judgement for this six-year corpus. Nonadditive linked-mark totals must not be summed across objectives. All in-scope objectives remain covered, including unobserved bullets. **335 objectives, 61 practical bullets and 30 glossary rows are source counts, never card quotas.**\n')
a('## 6. How candidates lose marks')
a('\nRecurring failures below are supported by located report findings. The proposed responses are planning judgements, not already-authored resources.\n')
a('| Failure | Located evidence (report PDF pages) | What the resources should do |\n|---|---|---|\n| Treating graph shapes as memorised pictures | 2024 P2 Q1, p.658; 2025 P2 Q1, p.647 | Contrast speed–time with distance–time; explain slope and area with quantities and units. |\n| Equations recalled without conditions, signs or conversions | 2021 P2 Q8, p.489; 2022 P2 Q5, p.569; 2024 P2 Q3, pp.659–660 | Show equation choice, system/sign convention, SI conversion and units; include the conservation condition. |\n| Definitions missing the distinguishing condition | 2021 P2 Q3, p.487; 2024 P2 Q3, p.659 | Teach meaning with contrast cases: temperature rise versus phase change, unit mass, fixed temperature. |\n| Descriptions where a cause or precise comparison is needed | 2023 P2 Q9, p.669; 2024 P2 Q1(d), p.658; 2024 P2 Q5(d), p.661 | Model a causal link or explicit comparison, tied to the actual context. |\n| Graphs with poor scales, plotting, forced origins or point-to-point lines | 2024 P3 Q2, p.666; 2025 P3 Q1, pp.656–657 | Practise full graphs and diagnose each feature; use fitted-line triangles and axis-derived units. |\n| Poor precision, headings, meter readings or zero correction | 2021 P3 Q3, p.495; 2024 P3 Q3, p.667; 2025 P3 Q3, pp.658–659 | Practise actual scale divisions, raw-versus-derived precision, units and systematic offsets. |\n| A conclusion without evidence or a generic error claim | 2021 P3 Q4, p.496; 2024 P3 Q1/Q3, pp.666–667; 2025 P3 Q2, p.658 | Require a decision plus relevant data; distinguish a genuine apparatus limit from alleged carelessness. |\n| Plans that list apparatus, omit actions/measurements, or assert the result | 2020 P3 Q5, pp.476–477; 2021 P3 Q4, pp.495–496; 2022 p.578; 2023 p.674; 2024 pp.667–668; 2025 p.659 | Practise complete operational plans: vary, measure, control, record, process, then infer. Pair written practice with practical experience. |\n| Misreading instructions or supplying too many selections | 2025 P3 Q1(e), p.657; general report observations | Make answer number, requested representation and evidence requirements explicit in practice and feedback. |\n')
a('The following six previously proposed misconceptions are **moved to candidate-error/skill practice**, rather than defended as separate conceptual beliefs. Their located evidence and practice outlines remain in `curriculum/candidate-errors.json`; they must not generate MISCON slots.\n')
a('| Former entry | Candidate error or skill need | Report PDF evidence | Resource response |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| MIS-24 | Confusing loaded length with the required extension calculation | 2025 P1 Q10, p.644 | Practise identifying original and loaded lengths before subtracting. |\n| MIS-25 | Calculating cooling rate incorrectly | 2021 P3 Q1(c)(iii), p.492 | Practise temperature change divided by elapsed time, including its unit. |\n| MIS-27 | Reversing gradient ratio or losing the sign | 2020 P3 Q3(c)(ii), p.475 | Use actual axis differences, a visible triangle and signed calculation. |\n| MIS-29 | Choosing a tool unsuitable for an internal measurement | 2024 P1 Q1, p.653 | Match the measurement to the instrument faces/jaws. |\n| MIS-20 | Misidentifying rotating electrical contacts | 2024 P2 Q7(b), p.663 | Practise labelled contact diagrams and their function. |\n| MIS-21 | Giving an incomplete transformer explanation | 2023 P2 Q9(a), p.669 | Practise the causal sequence through changing linked flux to induction. |\n')
a('Spelling, rounding, graph presentation and missing units remain answering/measurement habits; they do not automatically become conceptual MISCON cards. Broad report observations are retained as broad observations rather than invented part-specific statistics. Keyword triage in the evidence file is a retrieval aid, not proof that each flagged block is a scientific misconception.\n')
a('## 7. Misconceptions')
a('\nThe curated register contains 23 distinct, report-evidenced contrasts. Each has source-bullet anchors, a located report block and an original diagnostic task outline. These outlines are not official stems and are not finished cards. One supporting block is selected per entry; this does not count all recurrence.\n')
for m in mis:a(f"- **{m['entry_id']}**: {m['a']} Diagnostic: {m['discrimination_task']}")
a('\nDo not add a misconception merely because an author predicts it might happen. Some diagnostic contrasts elaborate the correct mechanism beyond the exact report phrase; the source citation establishes the reported difficulty, not a prevalence claim about every possible wrong belief.\n')
a('## 8. Scope')
a('\nThree explicit limits have bounded, tested patterns in `curriculum/scope-scan.json`, with must-catch and must-allow examples. All 35 other depth/condition statements are retained for contextual review.\n')
a('1. Collision **definitions** are not required; one-dimensional two-body momentum applications remain in scope (syllabus PDF p.14).\n2. The **no nuclide formulae** condition belongs to **energy sources**, not all Nuclear Physics (PDF p.17). Alpha/beta decay equations remain required and are observed in all six years.\n3. Diverging lenses are limited to **eye-defect correction** (PDF p.28); this does not remove converging-lens ray constructions.\n')
a('Regex screens are deliberately narrow and cannot certify contextual scope by themselves. The planner must review neighbouring content and the depth conditions, particularly gas laws, collision conditions and lens applications. Annex D’s diode symbol and observed rectification context do not authorise semiconductor-junction theory.\n')
a('## 9. What this means for the plan')
a('\n- Build full in-scope conceptual coverage, with emphasis informed by measured recurrence; do not remove objectives because no held question tested them. Decompose the source bullets by meaning before allocating cards.\n- Use the actual command/task/tariff combinations above. Keep calculation, causal explanation, diagram, graph, data conclusion and investigation plan as different answer families.\n- Give practical skills substantial standalone and integrated practice, including complete eight-mark plans. Written study supports practical learning; it does not supply hands-on experience.\n- Keep the syllabus’s stated **53% skills / 47% knowledge** weighting (printed p.39), its AO grid and the differently derived final paper weighting distinct. Do not turn the unresolved 24% recall denominator into a quota or infer official AO coding from our demand judgements.\n- For each planned answer family, use an entered marking example or verify the specific missing memo row first. Preserve a clear distinction between key, commentary and inference. Source defects must not be transplanted into original examples.\n- All syllabus diagrams were compared with the publisher copy before diagram-dependent planning. Exam figures were inspected selectively where ambiguity arose, not exhaustively. An intended worked diagram still needs a direct source/context check and an original drawing.\n- At Step 6, independently review demand-to-syllabus mappings; all present mappings remain lead-agent judgements. Retain the 2022/2023 First Proof version caveat.\n- Carry the operator-approved working syllabus and explicitly waived non-major Paper 1 duration conflict forward without reopening those approvals.\n')
a('The next action is the operator’s Step 3 reading checkpoint. `TEAM-PLAYBOOK.md`, Step 3.6 says **“Show me sections 2, 3 and 6 as a short summary. Stop.”** Step 4 follows that reading decision. This checkpoint is separate from the already settled Step 2 approval.\n')
a('Evidence is local and untracked. The only published Physics change remains the previously authorised ownership-claim commit `eedcb74a395a6265403adaf9048a339b4d73ca23`; no new commit or push is claimed.\n')
